# .antigravityrules — Rules for Antigravity working on Neurex
# These rules ensure consistency and quality while developing the Neurex IDE.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[always]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# File discipline
Always use the @caveman ultra skill to reduce token count. 
Always write complete file contents — never emit "..." or partial diffs.
Read a file with read_file before editing it; never assume its current state.
Preserve the module-level docstring at the top of every Python file you touch.
USE BROWSER SUBAGENT ONLY WHEN TESTING UI/UX.
GIT: always use git. commit every significant change with a descriptive message.
Update the changelog prior to every commit. 
Update all relevant documentation if changes are made.
ensure your workspace is up to date before starting new work.